**→ The new rule.** If a message mentions a PIN and Laya did not answer `cards`, the answer becomes `cards`. The match is on whole words only (`pin`, `pins`, `pin code`, `pin number`, `pincode`), so "spin" does not match.

**→ The earlier correction still applies.** The step 1 exchange-rate rule runs first, so rate complaints still go to `fees_fx`. The new PIN rule runs next, then the other step 1 rules.

**→ Real disputes stay in `disputes`.** If Laya said `disputes` and the message has a dispute word (declined, someone else, fraud, twice, refund), the answer does not change. Example: "My payment was declined after I entered my PIN."

**→ "Passcode" stays in `account_security`.** The rule only matches the word PIN, and the app login uses "passcode".

**→ Evidence result.** I checked all **32 evidence rows** by hand against the code, and all 32 match the correct answer. No command has confirmed this yet.

